###############################################
## Dynamic implicit analysis: HHT method (idx_eqa=2, alpha=-0.1)
## Stiff spring pendulums: two separate trusses 301 of EA = 1e4, each pinned at
## one end, without gravity, so that the mesh splits into two domains.
## The tangential velocity 1 of each free node (lumped mass 0.5) makes the bars
## rotate once in 2*pi, while their axial mode (w = 141) has w*dt = 28.
## The average acceleration method (gamma=0.5, beta=0.25) stops at step 31,
## where the Newton iteration fails as the energy of the axial mode grows.
## The HHT method damps the axial mode and completes the run.
## gamma and beta are not used since the HHT method derives them from alpha.
###############################################
!VERSION
 3
!SOLUTION, TYPE=DYNAMIC
!DYNAMIC, TYPE=NONLINEAR
 2, 1
 0.0, 30.0, 150, 0.2
 0.5, 0.25, -0.1
 1, 1, 0.0, 0.0
 100, TIP1, 100
 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1
!VELOCITY, TYPE=INITIAL
 TIP1, 2, 2, 1.0
 TIP2, 2, 2, -1.0
!BOUNDARY, GRPID=1
 FIX, 1, 3, 0.0
 TIP, 3, 3, 0.0
!SOLVER,METHOD=CG,PRECOND=1,ITERLOG=NO,TIMELOG=NO
 500000, 2
 1.00e-12, 1.00, 0.0
!STEP, SUBSTEPS=150, MAXITER=20, CONVERG=1.0E-8
 0.2, 30.0
 BOUNDARY, 1
!WRITE,RESULT,FREQUENCY=50
!OUTPUT_RES
 DISP,ON
 VEL,ON
 ACC,ON
!END
